  "headline": "Funeral Arrangements Announced For Senior Politician Panda Nababan",
  "seoTitle": "Panda Nababan Funeral Details Announced",
  "metaDescription": "Following his death from leukemia, senior Indonesian politician Panda Nababan will be laid to rest in North Tapanuli with traditional Batak rites.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Panda Nababan, a prominent senior politician and journalist, passed away on November 9, 2026, due to leukemia.",
    "His burial is scheduled for November 12, 2026, in Siborong-borong, North Tapanuli, North Sumatra, following traditional Batak funeral rites.",
    "Colleagues and public figures, including Meutya Hafid and Rano Karno, have paid tribute to his legacy as a mentor, journalist, and politician."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Panda Nababan was a well-known Indonesian figure recognized for his extensive career as both a dedicated journalist and a senior politician associated with the Indonesian Democratic Party of Struggle (PDIP). He was frequently described by his peers as a persistent fighter with a strong sense of integrity. Following his death on November 9, 2026, due to leukemia, political figures and media professionals have publicly reflected on his influence as a mentor. His family and party members have confirmed that his final resting place will be a family cemetery in Siborong-borong, North Tapanuli, North Sumatra. The interment ceremony is slated for November 12, 2026, and will incorporate traditional Batak funeral customs. During his final days, he reportedly remained engaged with contemporary political issues, including recent legal developments involving high-level government figures.",
